_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 17
---
order: 17
---
short_label: VI.17
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If three straight lines are proportional, then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the square on the mean; and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the square on the mean, then the three straight lines are proportional.
----
proof:

Let the three straight lines {A} and {B} and {C} be proportional, so that {A} is to {B} as {B} is to {C}.

I say that the rectangle {A} by {C} equals the square on {B}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="160" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
